                <pb facs="0916" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 T 79/71: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-22T14:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 22,
                                1923—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 23—9:52
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. The secretary of the recently established Vladivostok department of the Moscow
                    Commissariat for Foreign Affairs has notified me that three months is allowed me
                    to obtain official exequatur by negotiation between the United States and the
                    People’s Commissariat for Foreign Affairs at Moscow. This consulate may function
                    in the meantime although the Soviet authorities will not recognize it as
                    official. The Chinese, Japanese and British consuls have received communications
                    of the same purport.</p>
                <p>Possibly if no action is taken the Soviet authorities will allow me to remain as
                    a private individual. However, it is likely that the consulate will not be
                    permitted to function as in the past, even unofficially. Pending definite
                    instructions I will leave the Soviet communication unanswered.</p>
                <p>I have informed the Embassy at Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
